            <profile id="c4d7-db99-8422-ff5a" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword, light armour, shield. May be mounted on a horse (+8 pts) or a warhorse (+16 pts). May have javelins (+2 pts), throwing spear or thrusting spear (+2 pts). May wear heavy armour (+1 pt). If no other Army General is taken, a single Infante may be made Army General for +25 pts (in Asturias &amp; the Early Christian Kingdoms the Army General may only be an Infante). Asturias: characters may not wear heavy armour or ride warhorses. Reconquista: may have a lance (+4 pts) and horse barding (+2 pts). (El Cid p.12)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="d914-0fc5-68f5-ca1e" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
