  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="1a01-a465-cd36-2158" name="Christian Spain (El Cid) - List Notes" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false">
      <description>CHRISTIAN SPAIN ARMY LIST (El Cid, pp.7-16): Asturias &amp; the Early Christian Kingdoms (c.900-1040), the Age of El Cid (c.1040-1100) and the Reconquista (c.1100-1250). Percentages are by points. Special rules p.9 (Bloodthirsty).
Each troop type belongs to a Common or Uncommon pool that depends on the composition chosen; the units therefore also belong to pool categories named after the composition. Andalusian Allies are documented only (no pick list). Not enforced: mixed weapons within a unit, the Andalusian Allies percentages, and "may have up to 50% Arqueros" in combined units.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Asturias]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Asturias: at least 33%
  Uncommon Troops: Asturias: up to 33%
  Asturias &amp; the Early Christian Kingdoms, c.900-1040 AD (pp.9-10; Asturias, Leon, Galicia, Navarre, Aragon, Castile). Characters up to 25%: Infante, Armiger, Cantador, Bishop (no Rey); the Army General may only be an Infante. Characters cannot wear heavy armour or ride warhorses. Common Troops at least 33%: Jinetes, Caballeros, Peones, Arqueros, Skirmishers, Basque Javelinmen. Uncommon Troops up to 33%: Mercenary Spearmen, Archers and Jinetes. Andalusian Allies (up to 25%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers, from the Al-Andalus list; they become Aliados y Mercenarios) are not built.
[El Cid]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: El Cid: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: El Cid: up to 33%
  The Age of El Cid, c.1040-1100 AD (p.10). Characters up to 25% (Rey, Infante, Armiger, Cantador, Bishop; the Army General may be a Rey or an Infante). Common Troops at least 50%: Jinetes, Caballeros, Caballeros Hidalgos, Caballeros Villanos, Skirmishers. Uncommon Troops up to 33%: Guard Spearmen, Peones, Arqueros, Ballesteros, Militia Crossbowmen (0-1 unit only), Mercenary Spearmen, Archers and Jinetes, Basque Javelinmen. Andalusian Allies (up to 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers) are not built.
[Reconquista]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Reconquista: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: Reconquista: up to 33%
  The Reconquista, c.1100-1250 AD (pp.10-11). Characters up to 25% (Rey, Infante, Armiger, Cantador, Bishop; the Army General may be a Rey or an Infante). Common Troops at least 50%: Jinetes, Caballeros, Caballeros Hidalgos, Caballeros Villanos, Caballeros de las Ordenes Militares, Guard Spearmen, Peones, Arqueros, Skirmishers, Militia Crossbowmen. Uncommon Troops up to 33%: Ballesteros, Basque Javelinmen, Mercenary Spearmen, Archers and Jinetes. Special rules: the Bishop may be upgraded to a Crusading Bishop (+40 pts); mounted characters and Caballeros Hidalgos may have horse barding (+2 pts); Caballeros Villanos can ride warhorses (+4 pts per model); Jinetes, Peones, Arqueros and Basque Javelinmen may have light armour (+2 pts per model); Hidalgos may exchange spears for lances (+4 pts), Villanos (+2 pts); any character except the Armiger may take a lance (+4 pts). Andalusian Allies (up to 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Knights, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers, Crossbowmen, Mounted Crossbowmen) are not built.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
